      "response": {
        "category": "correctness",
        "consequence": "The `queued` value does not show when the assignment was queued. Any later logic or debugging that relies on it sees a wrong time, and it can be hours or days old.",
        "evidence_refs": [
          "source:new:src/sentry/integrations/services/assignment_source.py@sha256:885ab5f3b8ef5398cf84e90112d9352978908c663d9034ef89e7ed4eccfdfa0e"
        ],
        "explanation": "The dataclass field `queued: datetime = timezone.now()` calls `timezone.now()` once, when the module is imported. `from_integration` never passes `queued`, so every AssignmentSource built in a long-running worker or web process gets the same stale timestamp, which is the process start time. `to_dict()` then serializes that stale value into the task kwargs.",
        "lines": {
          "end_line": 18,
          "start_line": 18
        },
